# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output. The Content-Security-Policy is
# not here: Astro emits it as a `<meta http-equiv>` with the hashes of the inline scripts
# it just built (see `security.csp` in `astro.config.mjs`), which is the only version of
# the policy that cannot go stale. What is left are the headers a meta tag cannot carry.
# `Strict-Transport-Security` is a day, not a year, and carries neither
# `includeSubDomains` nor `preload`: the browser caches HSTS for the whole `max-age`, so
# a wrong value is not something a redeploy can take back. Raise it once this has run for
# a while without a plain-HTTP surprise. `Permissions-Policy` denies the features a
# static portfolio never asks for, and with them anything ever embedded here.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=()

# Content-hashed by the build, and the fonts are versioned by their file name: safe to
# keep for a year. Everything else falls back to the Pages default, which revalidates.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
